From: user <user@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wxQt iOS: dialog titlebar strip is click-through except its buttons (round 17, Job O sweep)

Sean widened round 17's Job O from dialogs to the whole app.
The sweep cleared panes, toolbars, status bars, splitters,
menus-by-construction and every editor frame at the 0.6
workspace, but convicted the round-17 overlay itself (wx
0025): the strip is opaque, full-width and raised across the
top 44 px of every dialog, and wx 0024's topmost arbitration
leaves two regimes -- strip topmost: content beneath is
invisible and untappable; strip covered: content works but
the strip's Minimize/Close are dead. Interactive content
provably lives in that band: the LIB_TREE Filter row's cancel
X and sort gear (the symbol chooser), embedded WX_INFOBARs
built as a dialog's first sizer row (~15 dialog bases, ERC
and DRC included), and PCM's notebook tab row.

F1a from the sweep, implemented here: when the strip is
installed on a non-QMainWindow host, the strip widget and
its title label get Qt::WA_TransparentForMouseEvents and a
transparent repaint (title on a translucent scrim, buttons
unchanged and opaque). QApplication::widgetAt() tests each
widget's own attribute, so the buttons -- which do not carry
it -- stay claimable through patch 0024's hit-test exactly
as before, while any other press in the band resolves to
the dialog content beneath and is delivered there: content
is visible and tappable, the strip's chrome still works,
and neither regime can recur. The strip's title-area drag
claim on dialogs dies with the band (frames keep their
layout-space strip and full drag; dialogs are clamped modal
sheets). A wxLogTrace literal (jobo2-strip-clickthrough)
marks the path in the shipped binary.

Signed-off-by: user <user@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/qt/toplevel.cpp
+++ b/src/qt/toplevel.cpp
@@ -1510,7 +1510,53 @@
             // overlay trade is the one round 16 already accepted
             // in practice: any wx relayout undid the shift anyway.
             if ( tb.strip->parentWidget() != host )
+            {
                 tb.strip->setParent( host );
+
+                // [KiCad-IOS port] Added 2026-11-09 for iOS (round
+                // 17, Job O sweep, wx patch 0026): as an overlay
+                // the strip must not eat the dialog's top band.
+                // The whole-app sweep proved interactive content
+                // lives in that band -- the LIB_TREE Filter row's
+                // cancel X and sort gear, embedded info bars
+                // posted as a dialog's first sizer row, notebook
+                // tab rows -- and an opaque, press-claiming strip
+                // leaves it invisible and untappable whenever the
+                // strip is topmost. So on dialogs the strip and
+                // its title become transparent to mouse events:
+                // QApplication::widgetAt() (the 0024 hit-test)
+                // tests each widget's own attribute, so the
+                // strip's buttons, which do not carry it, stay
+                // claimable exactly as before, while a press
+                // anywhere else in the band resolves to the
+                // dialog content beneath and is delivered there.
+                // (The strip's title-area drag claim dies with
+                // the band -- widgetAt() no longer resolves a
+                // band press to the strip. Dialogs are clamped
+                // modal sheets; frames keep their layout-space
+                // strip and full drag.) Visually the full-width
+                // opaque band goes too: the strip paints nothing,
+                // the title sits on a translucent scrim, and only
+                // the buttons stay opaque.
+                tb.strip->setAttribute( Qt::WA_TransparentForMouseEvents,
+                                        true );
+                tb.title->setAttribute( Qt::WA_TransparentForMouseEvents,
+                                        true );
+                tb.strip->setStyleSheet( QStringLiteral(
+                    "QWidget { background-color: transparent; }"
+                    "QLabel { color: white;"
+                    "         background-color: rgba(24, 24, 28, 150);"
+                    "         font-size: 15px; }"
+                    "QPushButton { color: white;"
+                    "              background-color: rgb(62, 62, 68);"
+                    "              border: none; border-radius: 7px;"
+                    "              padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 15px; }"
+                    "QPushButton:pressed { background-color: rgb(96, 96, 104); }"
+                    "QPushButton:checked { background-color: rgb(10, 110, 220); }" ) );
+                wxLogTrace( "kicad-ios-round17",
+                            "jobo2-strip-clickthrough: dialog strip "
+                            "installed click-transparent except buttons" );
+            }
             wxLogTrace( "kicad-ios-round17",
                         "jobo-titlebar-overlay-only: dialog strip "
                         "installed without resize" );
